                <pb facs="0973" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/84: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stockton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-20T17:00:00+01:00">January 20, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 20—1:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Department’s telegram 45, December 8, 6 p.m. Forwarding pouch tomorrow
                    Austrian Government’s acceptance Senate reservation and <pb facs="0974" n="860"
                        xml:id="pg860"/> supplemental article signed today. Urge Senate’s consent to
                    supplemental article be obtained earliest possible date. Will press for
                    immediate ratification by Austrian Parliament.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
